nd please don't share it on screen like I just did. Now let's write the main script."},{"startMs":45100,"endMs":59900,"transcript":"We load the key with Dondov and read the notes file from the the first argument. Then we call the chat endpoint with with the wrong sorry let me say that that again. Then we call the chat completions endpoint with the model name and a short system prompt."},{"startMs":59900,"endMs":64780,"transcript":"Finally, we print the summary. Let's try it on a real meeting."},{"startMs":65020,"endMs":107020,"transcript":"And there it is, three bullet points, and a list of action items. That took about, four seconds, which is fast enough for me. One more thing, if the file is missing, the script crashes with a pretty ugly stack trace. so let's add a small error handler error handler that prints a friendly message instead and now when I run it again with the wrong file name we get one clear line let me quickly recap we installed two packages stored the key in a dot env file and called the chat completions endpoint with our notes in the next video I'll add streaming so the summary shows up up word by word thanks for for watching and you know see you next time"}]}